<title>GERMANY: BfG says chairman Wieandt retires.</title>
<headline>BfG says chairman Wieandt retires.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's BfG Bank said on Wednesday that its management board chairman Paul Wieandt was retiring from the board.</p>
<p>In a brief statement, the bank said Wieandt's departure was retroactive to March 31.</p>
<p>&quot;The supervisory board of BfG Bank AG  BFGG.F has agreed to Dr Paul Wieandt's request that he be allowed to retire with effect from March 31, 1997,&quot; the statement said.</p>
